# Apple UI Design System & HIG Rules

When designing, implementing, or auditing UI for iOS, iPadOS, macOS, visionOS, watchOS, or Apple-style web/cross-platform apps, follow these rules:

## 1. System Controls First
- Prefer native system components (`Button`, `Toggle`, `Picker`, `TabView`, `NavigationSplitView`, `List`, `Menu`, `ContentUnavailableView`) over custom-drawn shapes.
- Map kit variant axes to native modifiers (e.g. `Size` → `.controlSize()`, `Style` → `.buttonStyle()`, `Destructive` → `role: .destructive`, `Disabled` → `.disabled()`).
- On web, start with standard HTML semantic elements (`<button>`, `<input type="checkbox" role="switch">`, `<select>`, `<dialog>`).

## 2. Colors & Typography
- **Never hardcode hex values** for system UI. Always use semantic colors:
  - **SwiftUI**: `Color.primary`, `.secondary`, `Color(.systemBackground)` (iOS) or `Color(nsColor: .windowBackgroundColor)` (macOS). Accent colors via `.tint()`.
  - **React Native**: `PlatformColor('label')`, `PlatformColor('secondarySystemGroupedBackground')`.
  - **Web**: CSS variables `var(--label)`, `var(--bg)`, `var(--tint)`, `var(--separator)` from `skills/apple-ui-web/references/tokens.css` or Tailwind classes from `skills/apple-ui-web/references/tailwind-theme.css`.
- Honor Dynamic Type and system text styles (`.font(.largeTitle)`, `.headline`, `.body`, etc.). Never fix font sizes without `@ScaledMetric`.

## 3. Liquid Glass (26-Series)
- Liquid Glass belongs exclusively in the **controls and navigation layer** (floating toolbars, tab bars, grabber surfaces), never behind content text or cards.
- Never stack glass upon glass. Group adjacent floating controls in `GlassEffectContainer` so materials merge seamlessly.
- Always provide fallbacks for `prefers-reduced-transparency` and browsers/platforms lacking `backdrop-filter`.

## 4. Platform-Specific Conventions
- **iOS & iPadOS**:
  - Minimum hit target: 44 x 44 pt.
  - Top-level navigation: `TabView` with `.tabBarMinimizeBehavior(.onScrollDown)` and `.tabViewStyle(.sidebarAdaptable)`.
  - Search: `Tab(role: .search)` or `.searchable(text:)`.
  - Modal tasks: `.sheet` with `.presentationDetents([.medium, .large])` and `.presentationDragIndicator(.visible)`.
- **macOS**:
  - App-level structure: `NavigationSplitView` with `.listStyle(.sidebar)` and `.toolbar`.
  - Push buttons: Mark the primary default action with `.keyboardShortcut(.defaultAction)`.
- **visionOS**:
  - Minimum hit target: 60 x 60 pt with minimum 16 pt margins between items.
  - Controls: Attach window actions via `.ornament(attachmentAnchor: .scene(.bottom))`.
  - Gaze feedback: Every custom control must support `.hoverEffect(.highlight)`.
- **watchOS**:
  - Navigation: Vertical carousel lists (`.listStyle(.carousel)`) linked to `.digitalCrownRotation`.
  - Actions: Capsule buttons at the bottom of the screen (`.buttonBorderShape(.capsule)`).

## 5. Licensing & Artwork Guardrails
- Do **not** export, extract, or commit Apple Design Resources binary artwork, `.fig` files, or SF font files.
- Refer to SF Symbols by system name (`systemImage: "..."`). On web/Android, use generic licensed icons.
- Clearly state that web, Android, and cross-platform outputs are approximations outside Apple-OS software.
